                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While I respect it, both for it's age and it's ambition, SEIV is just...dull.\n\nWhile in THEORY you can do a lot...you are shockingly limited in what you can do in practice and that's where it all falls apart.\n\nYou see its sprawling list of technologies and are supposed to imagine making ringworlds and fleets of baseships, but getting there is such a nightmare slog of repetition and iteration that the game can only sell off of nostalgia, which...\n\nIs there nostalgia for this? I know for a while it was a big name in town, but only because, what, there were like three names in the 4X business?\n\nThe game, seen critically, is rough, to the point where I wonder how it even got to be a franchise. It's easy to see why the name is basically dead.\n\nI'm not mad, but how could I be? Doing literally no research on the matter it feels like this was just some passion project for a guy in his basement back when that was a viable business model.\n\nI respect it, in many ways, but not as a game. You don't need to visit this for yourself.",
